# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example environment configuration for ink-capture.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
# Keep this file up to date as new required variables are introduced.
# All values below are placeholders/commented out — nothing here is a real secret.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Recognition (vision) backend ---------------------------------------------
# API key for the cloud recognition backend, if/when a cloud vision API
# (e.g. Scrydex Vision) is the selected CardRecognizer. Pending confirmation —
# see CLAUDE.md "ask-first" rules before adopting a paid backend.
# RECOGNITION_API_KEY=your-recognition-api-key-here

# Optional: override the recognition service base URL.
# RECOGNITION_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example-vision-service.com

# Optional: force the StubCardRecognizer instead of the on-device OCR backend.
# Set to `true` (or `1`) to skip ML Kit OCR and wire an empty stub recognizer —
# handy for manual runs on a simulator with no camera, or to isolate a bug to the
# OCR path. Unset (or any other value) uses the real OCR recognizer. Read via
# react-native-config (visionConfig.ts); a non-secret flag, but `.env` stays
# git-ignored.
# USE_STUB_RECOGNIZER=true

# --- Card catalog -------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional override for the LorcanaJSON catalog base URL. The app defaults to the
# canonical base below in code (DEFAULT_CATALOG_BASE_URL), so this is only needed
# to point at a mirror or a pinned snapshot. B2's CatalogService fetches
# `${base}/metadata.json` + `${base}/allCards.json` and caches them on-device;
# bulk card data is fetched at runtime, never bundled. Read via
# react-native-config — a non-secret value, but `.env` stays git-ignored.
# (Lorcast remains a future SECONDARY source for on-demand images/prices and
# would get its own var when added.)
# CATALOG_API_BASE_URL=https://lorcanajson.org/files/current/en
